Let $n>1$ be a positive integer. Each square unit of a grid of squares $n \times n$ is coloured in black or white, so that the following conditions apply:
- The two black squares may be connected by a sequence of black squares where each successive square of the sequence shares an edge;
- The two white squares may be connected by a sequence of white squares where both consecutive squares of the sequence share an edge;
- Each subnet $2 \times 2$ contains at least one square of each colour.

Determine, with evidence, the maximum possible difference between the number of black and white squares in this grid (in terms of $n$) .

